add('Escape probability inversion needs a rate reference scale','rare-event formulas','2025-12-10','U','Probability and dimensions','What assumptions make the recovered probability-to-barrier inversion valid?',
'The recovered scalarengine inverted an exponential exit law and identified its result with a geometric barrier. This is exact only for an assumed constant-hazard model,and a logarithm of a dimensional rate requires a reference prefactor.',
['For a constant rateλ>0,an exponential waiting time satisfiesP_t=P(τ≤t)=1−e^(−λt).','AnArrheniusmodel isλ=λ₀e^(−W/ε),withλ₀andλhaving the same time-inverse units.'],
'Exact rate and barrier inversion','If0<P_t<1,thenλ=−log(1−P_t)/tandW=−εlog[−log(1−P_t)/(tλ₀)]. The factorλ₀cannot be omitted unless a dimensionless time convention fixes it toone.',
'Solving1−P_t=e^(−λt)by logarithms gives the rate. Dividingλbyλ₀in theArrheniusrelation gives a dimensionless quantity whose logarithm is−W/ε. This proves the formula,with no approximation. The exponential distribution has constant hazard because its survival ratioS(t+s)/S(t)=e^(−λs)depends only ons. A general first-passage distribution need not have this memoryless property,and a small-noise exit asymptotic does not assert an exact exponential law at every time. The derivative ofWwith respect toP_tis−ε/[tλ₀·(−log(1−P_t)/(tλ₀))·(1−P_t)],showing ill-conditioning near the endpoints.',
'Taket=2,λ₀=1in chosen reciprocal-time units,andP_t=1−e^(−1).',
'Thenλ=1/2andW=εlog2. If the time unit changes,the numericalrate andλ₀both rescale,leavingλ/λ₀andWunchanged. Omittingλ₀would make the inferred barrier depend on a unit choice.',
'The scalar inversion is a valid model calculation once the hazard and prefactor are stated.',
'No general identityΔV=W/√detgwas recovered from a coordinate-invariant action;detgchanges under reparametrization. A first-cumulant correction requires a proved response map,not a dimensional guess.',
'Fit and test the full survival curve against a constant-hazard model,then propagate uncertainty through the logarithmic inversion with explicit prefactor uncertainty.',
[('Freidlin and Wentzell, exit asymptotics framework','https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-25847-3')])
add('Abel–Liouville controls volume,not every mode','Abel’s identity','2025-12-09','U','Linear differential equations','What does Abel’s identity prove for the recovered two-component stress model?',
'The recovered application correctly describedAbel–Liouvilleas structural rather than predictive. A two-dimensional linear system gives an exact determinant law and demonstrates why volume contraction does not imply stability of every direction.',
['LetX′=A(t)XwithX(0)=Iand continuousA.','For a constant symmetric model useA=[[-α,κ],[κ,−β]].'],
'Liouville determinant and sharp two-mode stability','detX(t)=exp(∫₀ᵗtrA(s)ds). Forα,β>0,the constant symmetric model is asymptotically stable exactly whenκ²<αβ.',
'Jacobi’s determinant formula givesd(detX)/dt=detX·tr(X^(−1)X′)=detX·trAas long asXis invertible. Solving the scalar equation gives the displayed positive exponential,which also guarantees invertibility for the full interval and completes the argument. For the symmetric matrix,the eigenvalues are−(α+β)/2±√((α−β)²/4+κ²). Both are negative exactly when the square root is smaller than(α+β)/2,equivalentlyκ²<αβ. The trace is negative regardless ofκ,so a negative volume-growth exponent alone does not exclude an unstable positive eigenvalue.',
'Takeα=0.015,β=0.020andκ=0.010in one consistent inverse-time unit.',
'κ²=0.0001<αβ=0.0003,so both eigenvalues are negative anddetX=e^(−0.035t). Ifκis increased to0.030,the trace and determinant law remain the same butκ²=0.0009>0.0003and one eigenvalue ispositive. This distinction is exact and can be checked without simulation.',
'The identity supplies volume evolution and a separate spectral test supplies directional stability.',
'These coefficients are historical illustrative assumptions,not verified fault parameters or a rupture forecast. Nonlinear switching,forcing and constitutive laws can invalidate conclusions drawn from one linearization.',
'For time-varying coefficients,seek a common positive Lyapunov matrix or an exponential-dichotomy bound;the determinant alone cannot supply a uniform stability theorem.',
[('NIST DLMF linear differential equations','https://dlmf.nist.gov/1.13')])
add('Decimal remainders and the exact Koopman period','r_{n+1}=10','2025-12-12','A','Finite dynamics and number theory','When does a decimal remainder orbit havep−1modes,and how does its spectrum differ from an FFT fit?',
'The recovered prime dataset was interpreted through primitive roots and cyclic Koopman eigenvalues. The cycle length is the multiplicative order of10modp,which need not bep−1. This provides exact arithmetic against which anyPCAorFFTinterpretation must be checked.',
['For primepnot dividing10,letT(r)=10rmodp onF_p×.','Letd=ord_p(10),the least positive integer with10^d≡1modp.'],
'Cycle length and Koopman roots of unity','Every nonzero remainder orbit has lengthd,andF_p×splits into(p−1)/dcycles. On one cycle,the Koopman operatorUf=f∘Thas eigenvalues e^(2πik/d),k=0,…,d−1.',
'T^nr=rholds exactly when10^nr≡rmodp. Since r≠0it can be cancelled,giving10^n≡1;hence the orbit length isd. The disjoint cycles partitionp−1points. Label a cycle byr_j=10^jr₀,jmodd. The characterf_k(r_j)=e^(2πikj/d)satisfiesUf_k(r_j)=f_k(r_(j+1))=e^(2πik/d)f_k(r_j). These characters form a complete discrete Fourier basis. A digit observable can have zero coefficients in some eigendirections,so an FFTof one observable need not visibly show every Koopman eigenvalue. PCAorIsomapcoordinates further depend on the supplied dataset and metric.',
'Comparep=7andp=11.',
'Modulo7,the orbit1,3,2,6,4,5has length6=p−1. Modulo11,the orbit1,10has length2,so there arefivecycles and no single length-tenorbit. Both primes are perfectly valid inputs,but thefull-cycleformula only applies to the first. Artin’sprimitive-root conjecture is a separate global statement about how often orderp−1occurs.',
'The spectral period is exactly computable from modular arithmetic and cannot be assigned from the prime’s size alone.',
'The historical FFTpeak and entropy tables had no recovered raw digit arrays or normalization,so their numerical values and branch interpretation remain unverified.',
'Compute the exact orders for every recovered prime,then compare digit-observable Fourier coefficients using one declared sampling and entropy convention.',
[('NIST DLMF primitive roots and orders','https://dlmf.nist.gov/27.6')])
add('Softmax Fisher geometry and a uniform fixed-point diagnostic','empirical-Fisher','2025-12-22','U','Information geometry','Which diagnostics of uniform and concentrated predictions follow exactly from softmax geometry?',
'The recovered grokking logs reported near-uniform entropy, nearly constant Fisher weights and a vanishing update, followed by a highly concentrated run. The underlying probability geometry is exact, but it does not turn one telemetry pattern into a general grokking predictor.',
['For logitsu∈R^m,setp_i=e^(u_i)/Σe^(u_j). The categorical Fisher matrix isF=diag(p)−pp^T.','Entropy isH(p)=−Σp_i logp_i,andKL(q||p)=Σq_i log(q_i/p_i).'],
'Fisher null direction and local KL','F is positive semidefinite withF1=0. At the uniform distribution,p_i=1/m,F=(1/m)(I−11^T/m),andH=logm. For a small logit perturbationh,KL(p(u)||p(u+h))=(1/2)h^TFh+O(||h||³).',
'For everyv,v^TFv=Σp_iv_i²−(Σp_iv_i)²,which is the variance ofvunderp and hence nonnegative. Constants have zero variance, proving the null direction caused by invariance under adding a common logit. Differentiating the log-partitionA(u)=logΣe^(u_i)gives∇A=p and∇²A=F. The statedKL is A(u+h)−A(u)−p(u)·h;Taylor expansion gives the quadratic term. Substituting uniformp gives the exact projector formula and entropy. Thus a natural-gradient inverse requires restricting away from the constant direction or adding a specified regularizer.',
'Takem=97,as in the recovered modular-addition experiment.',
'Uniform entropy islog97≈4.574711,and every nonconstant Fisher eigenvalue is1/97. A diagonal-only normalized Fisher can look nearly constant without identifying the full Fisher spectrum. If an imposed schedule drives the step tozero,parameters can freeze at uniform prediction even though no useful solution was learned.',
'The diagnostic has exact mathematical anchors and a precise degeneracy that an optimizer must handle.',
'The historical validation accuracies and speedups cannot be reproduced without the programs,data and checkpoints. Low entropy alone may mean confident errors,and a tiny update does not certify convergence to a good solution.',
'Estimate the projected Fisher and actual KL per step,then compare prediction accuracy and held-out loss independently of the entropy or spectral diagnostic.',
[('Amari, natural gradient','https://doi.org/10.1162/089976698300017746')])
add('Mahalanobis proximal steps and what a tube projector preserves','Mahalanobis','2025-12-15','A','Convex optimization','What exact optimization problem underlies a tube-aligned proximal step?',
'The recovered optimizer narrative combined a Mahalanobis geometry, spectral tubes, a hostileℓ¹term and delayed commitment. A finite convex update is well-defined and solvable; a low-dimensional projection can also erase the entire useful gradient. Both facts can be proved without claiming an optimizer improvement.',
['LetM be symmetric positive definite. Considerargmin_d{g^Td+(1/(2η))d^TMd+λ||d||₁}.','LetP be an orthogonal projector onto a proposed retained subspace.'],
'Exact diagonal proximal solution and projection obstruction','IfM=diag(m_i),the minimizer isd_i=−(η/m_i)sign(g_i)max(|g_i|−λ,0). If a gradient lies inkerP,a projected updatePg iszero even when the objective is not stationary.',
'The diagonal objective separates by coordinate. On a positive or negative half-line,differentiation givesg_i+(m_i/η)d_i+λsign(d_i)=0;checking the subgradient interval atzero yields the soft-threshold formula. Strict convexity fromM>0makes the minimizer unique. For projection,ifPg=0then the projected iteration takes no descent direction althoughgmay be nonzero. For example the quadratic objectivef(x,y)=(x−1)²/2+(y−1)²/2at(1,0)has gradient(0,−1). Projecting onto thex-axis kills it,so the constrained point is stationary only within the chosen tube,not in the ambient problem.',
'TakeM=diag(1,4),η=1,g=(3,1),λ=2.',
'The update isd=(−1,0). The second coordinate is suppressed by thresholding,not by a proof that it is irrelevant. In the projection example a spectral gap or low turnover of the retained subspace cannot detect the losty-direction:the projector may remain perfectly stable while optimization stalls.',
'The finite update has an exact solution, and premature tube commitment has a concrete mathematical failure mode.',
'No theorem says that observed gap,spike,turnover or effective rank predicts a useful invariant optimization subspace. The reported negative-control failure is historical experimental evidence,not a universal result.',
'Prove a bound on the discarded gradient||(I−P)∇f|| and include it in the descent estimate before replacing an ambient optimizer by its projected version.',
[('Parikh and Boyd, Proximal Algorithms','https://web.stanford.edu/~boyd/papers/prox_algs.html')])
add('Quantization error and LayerNorm require a positive denominator','quantization triggered NaNs','2025-12-14','U','Numerical analysis','Which deterministic bounds can guard the recovered quantization and normalization pipeline?',
'The recovered run failed numerically after a tube verification and proposed scale floors and rollback. A scale floor is a mathematical domain condition; a code label or verifier score cannot replace it. Simple bounds locate the quantization and normalization sensitivities.',
['For a nonzero scale s,uniform nearest quantization isQ_s(x)=s round(x/s).','Layer normalization onR^m isLN_ε(x)=(x−mean(x)1)/√(m^(−1)||x−mean(x)1||²+ε),withε>0.'],
'Quantization and global normalization bounds','Coordinatewise|Q_s(x_i)−x_i|≤s/2 without clipping. The Jacobian norm ofLN_ε is at most1/√ε,so||LN_ε(x)−LN_ε(y)||≤||x−y||/√ε.',
'Nearest-integer rounding changes a scalar by at mostone half,proving the first bound after multiplication bys. ForLN,letP=I−11^T/m,z=Px,andv=||z||²/m. Its derivative is(1/√(v+ε))P−zz^T/[m(v+ε)^(3/2)]. On the centered subspace, directions perpendicular tozhave eigenvalue1/√(v+ε);thezdirection has eigenvalueε/(v+ε)^(3/2). The constant direction has eigenvaluezero. All are nonnegative and at most1/√ε. Integrating the derivative along the segment betweenxandygives the Lipschitz bound. Ifε=0,normalization is undefined for constant inputs and no global bound exists.',
'Takem=2,x=(a,a),and a quantization scale derived only frommax|x_i|.',
'Atx=0,a scale formula s=max|x|/(2^(b−1)−1)gives s=0,andx/scannot be evaluated. A strictly positive scale floor defines the map there. For a perturbation(δ,−δ),LN_εreturns(δ,−δ)/√(δ²+ε),showing the largest sensitivity nearzero variance.',
'The proposed safeguards have precise mathematical purposes and quantified effects.',
'Finite arithmetic overflow,clipping and mixed-precision accumulation need additional range analysis. A historical99.93%validation result is not a bound on all future runs or all numerical paths.',
'Propagate the quantization bound through every normalization and activation using actual local denominator lower bounds,then compare the certified error budget with the model’s decision margin.',
[('Higham, Accuracy and Stability of Numerical Algorithms','https://doi.org/10.1137/1.9780898718027')])
add('A noisy pitchfork has an exact barrier and a conditional Kramers law','noise-controlled pitchfork','2025-12-20','U','Bifurcation and stochastic dynamics','Which barrier and prefactor follow from the recovered quartic potential,and what remains a model of grokking?',
'The recovered framework proposed a pitchfork coordinate and a batch-size/learning-rate noise level. The potential’s critical points and barrier can be derived exactly. Relating them to training time requires an independently justified reduction and a small-noise asymptotic.',
['LetU(m)=m⁴/4−αm²/2 withα>0,and use dM=−U′(M)dt+√(2D)dW.','A local minimum has positiveU″;the intervening saddle in one dimension is a local maximum.'],
'Exact symmetric barrier','The minima arem_±=±√α,the saddle ism_s=0,andΔU=α²/4. The overdamped one-dimensional Kramers prefactor givesEτ∼(√2π/α)e^(α²/(4D))under its standard small-noise assumptions for a well-to-well transition, or an absorbing boundary strictly beyond the saddle.',
'U′=m(m²−α),so the critical points arezero and±√α. U″=3m²−αis−αat zero and2αat either minimum. The minimum value is−α²/4and the saddle valuezero,proving the barrier. Substituting these curvatures in2π/√(|U″(m_s)|U″(m_a))gives√2π/α. The exponential convention usesnoise√(2D);with√Dthe rate exponent would instead be2ΔU/D. For a saddle-node normal formU(x)=x³/3−κx,κ>0,the critical points±√κhave barrier4κ^(3/2)/3and curvature magnitudes2√κ,explaining the recoveredκ^(3/2)barrier andκ^(−1/2)prefactor scaling.',
'Takeα=2and assumeD=c₀η/B.',
'The exact barrier isone and the formal mean time is(π/√2)exp(B/(c₀η)). This exponential dependence is extremely sensitive to the assumed reduced-noise coefficient. Changing the neural coordinate or the fitted drift without rederiving the action can change the barrier.',
'The polynomial model and its scaling are mathematically coherent,while the connection to grokking remains conditional.',
'Kramers’formula is asymptotic,not an exact finite-noise identity. No recovered proof maps the full optimizer state to this scalar diffusion with the claimedc₀,drift and metastable wells.',
'Estimate the reduced drift and diffusion from independent trajectories,check the Markov approximation,and test the predicted barrier scaling over several noise levels before extrapolating training times.',
[('Bovier et al., metastability and sharp exit asymptotics','https://doi.org/10.1007/s00440-004-0343-z')])
add('The recovered oscillator has minimal continuous state dimension eight','Exact discussed curve','2025-12-22','U','Linear systems and realization theory','Can the exact eight-mode claim be proved from the recovered curve rather than declared by a certifier?',
'The exact curve isγ(t)=(cos t+(1/2)cos2t+(1/2)cos4t+(3/8)cos8t,2sin t−sin2t+sin4t−(3/4)sin8t). Its continuous linear realization has dimensioneight. This is a verifiable result independent of any claimed subdivision or motivic origin.',
['Writeγ=(x,y),with frequencies1,2,4,8.','A continuous linear realization isγ(t)=Ce^(At)v with constant real matrices;its derivative Hankel matrix has entriesx^(i+j)(0).'],
'Exact order-eight annihilator and minimality','Each coordinate is annihilated byP(D)=(D²+1)(D²+4)(D²+16)(D²+64)=D⁸+85D⁶+1428D⁴+5440D²+4096. The derivative-Hankel rank ofxiseight,so no lower-dimensional constant linear realization exists.',
'Each sinusoidal frequency solves its corresponding second-order factor,and the commuting factors annihilate their sum. Four real rotation blocks therefore construct an eight-dimensional realization. To prove minimality,write x(t)=Σ_(λ∈{±i,±2i,±4i,±8i})c_λe^(λt),whereeveryc_λis nonzero. Thenx^(n)(0)=Σc_λλ^n. The8×8Hankel matrix equalsVdiag(c_λ)V^T,whereV_jλ=λ^j. Its determinant is(∏c_λ)(∏_(λ<μ)(μ−λ)²),nonzero because the eightλare distinct. Anyd-dimensional realization factors every derivative Hankel matrix throughR^d,so its rank is at mostd. The rank-eight lower bound matches the construction.',
'Compute the exact derivative certificate and its sampling caveat.',
'The8×8determinant is3317490507809254951983513600000000;the9×9determinant iszero and the displayed recurrence holds for every derivative index. Discrete samples at stepΔtretain rankeight only if the eight numbers e^(±ikΔt),k=1,2,4,8,are distinct and no observable coefficient is lost. AtΔt=2πthe entire sampled curve is constant.',
'The original continuous eight-state claim is proved with an exact rank certificate and explicit aliasing conditions.',
'It is a minimal linear realization,not a universal nonlinear latent-dimension theorem. Topological indices alone do not impose the same rank lower bound on arbitrary nonlinear models.',
'For a chosen nonaliased sampling step,derive the exact discrete recurrence and compare finite noisy Hankel singular values against a perturbation bound rather than a fixed rank threshold.',
[('Kalman, mathematical description of linear dynamical systems','https://doi.org/10.1137/0301010')])
add('Exact windings of the recovered oscillator','tangent-line/Maslov','2025-12-22','U','Complex analysis and topology','Can the reported indices−4and−6be certified without trusting a sampled phase unwrap?',
'The recovered exact curve permits polynomial argument-principle certificates. Its tangent never vanishes,and the winding ofw=z+iz′is−6. The tangent winding itself is−2;the reported−4uses the explicitly stated doubled tangent-line convention.',
['Letz=x+iyfor the curve in the preceding entry andu=e^(it).','Usewind(f)=(1/(2π))Δargf for a nonvanishing2π-periodic complex function.'],
'Polynomial root counts and indices','γ′=(i/2)u^(−8)P(u),withP=−9+2u⁴−3u⁶+u⁷+3u⁹−u¹⁰+6u¹²−3u¹⁶. Also w=(1/16)u^(−8)Q(u),withQ=81−20u⁴+36u⁶−16u⁷+4u¹⁰−36u¹²+21u¹⁶. P has six zeros in the unit disk,Q has two,and neither has a unit-circle zero.',
'Convert every cosine and sine to u^k andu^(−k);differentiation multiplies the kth Laurent coefficient byik,giving the two displayed polynomials exactly. Their disk counts are certified by a strict integer recursion. For a real polynomialpwith leadinga,constantband reversalp#,if|a|>|b|reduce to(ap−bp#)/uand addone to the disk count;if|b|>|a|reduce tobp−ap#and addzero. At each step remove a common nonzero integer factor. A boundary zero ofpwould also be a boundary zero of the reduced polynomial. Reaching a nonzero constant therefore proves absence of boundary zeros inductively. On the circle|p|=|p#|,so Rouché gives the asserted count update. The attached exact recursion yields6and2. The argument principle then subtracts the Laurent pole order8,giving windγ′=−2andwindw=−6. There are also exact rational Bezout certificates U P+V P#=1 and U_Q Q+V_Q Q#=1. On the unit circle |P#|=|P|,so 1≤(||U||_coeff,1+||V||_coeff,1)|P|. The verified coefficients give |P|≥6/35 and |Q|≥1686436183047081060/2638949151339309251.',
'Compare the continuous certificate to the historical sampled minima.',
'The Bezout bounds prove |γ′|≥3/35 and |w|>1/26, independently of the sampled minima. Uniform perturbations of the two respective complex functions by less than these margins preserve their windings: the straight-line homotopy stays away from zero by the triangle inequality. With the conventionμ=Δargγ′/π=2windγ′,the Maslov-style integer is−4. Using the ordinary vector winding instead gives−2,so the convention is essential.',
'The two historical indices are supported by exact finite algebra,with the doubling convention made explicit.',
'The certificate establishes no Catmull–Clark source,quantum state,or motivic quotient. These Laurent-polynomial facts are properties of the recovered curve itself.',
'Classify which coefficient deformations can cross the unit-root discriminant, and compare those genuine topological transitions with the independent continuous-realization rank and sampling-aliasing discriminants.',
[('NIST DLMF argument principle and Rouché theorem','https://dlmf.nist.gov/1.10')])
add('A capped-addition monoid with an exact trace ideal','29-mode','2025-12-31','U','Finite algebra','What general monoid theorem survives when the historical29×29operation table is unavailable?',
'The recovered source claimed exact closure,trace law,generators,idempotents and collision counts for29modes,but did not recover the table. A capped-addition construction provides a proved replacement while leaving those specific historical counts unverified.',
['LetL_k={0,…,k}withi⊕j=min(i+j,k).','For a monoidSdefineM=S×L_kwith(s,i)·(t,j)=(st,i⊕j),andtr(s,i)=i.'],
'Associative capped product and absorbing trace layer','M is a monoid with identity(1_S,0),andtr(xy)=min(trx+try,k). The top layerS×{k}is a two-sided ideal. IfS is a group andk>0,the idempotents are exactly(1_S,0)and(1_S,k).',
'Capped addition is associative because both(i⊕j)⊕ℓandi⊕(j⊕ℓ)equalmin(i+j+ℓ,k). Its identity iszero. Product associativity and identity follow coordinatewise fromS. If either trace isk,the product trace isk,proving the ideal statement. In a group,s²=simpliess=1_S. The remaining equationmin(2i,k)=ihas onlyi=0ori=k:if0<i<k,either2i<kand2i≠i,or2i≥kandk≠i. This proves the idempotent characterization. More generalScontributes its own idempotents in those two layers.',
'TakeS=C₂={1,g}andk=2.',
'Mhas six elements,two in each trace layer. The element(g,1)has square(1,2)and cube(g,2);the trace saturates while the group coordinate keeps changing. There are exactlytwo idempotents. This illustrates why an absorbing trace ideal need not consist of absorbing individual elements.',
'The general construction has a complete proof and an exact small model,without falsely certifying the absent29-mode table.',
'The historical counts(1,2,5,8,13),ten idempotents and generator set{1,5,6,8}cannot be deduced from this product model and remain unverified. A finite table needs exhaustive associativity checks,not only closure and commutativity.',
'Recover the actual table,enumerate every triple for associativity,then compute ideals,generators,idempotents and trace collisions directly before formalizing the table inLean.',
[('Lean mathlib finite algebra documentation','https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Algebra/Group/Defs.html')])
add('A rigorous two-point-to-gradient inequality','Setup τ:T³','2025-12-24','U','Sobolev estimates','What precisely follows from the recovered finite-difference disorder statistic?',
'The recovered Navier–Stokes program contains a valid local geometric estimate. Its conversion to a weighted gradient lower bound requires an explicit intermittency factor;that factor is a hypothesis,not a consequence of unit-length directions.',
['Let τ:T³→S² be smooth, w∈L²(T³) nonnegative, and ρ_r∈L¹(R³) nonnegative with total mass one and support |h|≤2r. Evaluate torus functions periodically for h∈R³.','SetA(r)=∫∫w(x)w(x+h)[1−(τ(x)·τ(x+h))²]ρ_r(h)dhdx.'],
'Exact weighted FTC–Jensen bound','A(r)≤4r²∫||∇τ(y)||²J_r(y)dy,whereJ_r(y)=ess sup_(s∈[0,1])∫w(y−sh)w(y+(1−s)h)ρ_r(h)dh. If J_r≤C_int w² almost everywhere for a finite C_int>0, then ∫w²||∇τ||²≥A(r)/(4r²C_int).',
'For unit vectorsu,v,1−(u·v)²=(1−u·v)(1+u·v)≤2(1−u·v)=||u−v||². Along the straight torus displacementh,the fundamental theorem givesτ(x+h)−τ(x)=∫₀¹∇τ(x+sh)h ds. Jensen bounds its squared norm by|h|²∫₀¹||∇τ(x+sh)||²ds. Insert this inA,use|h|²≤4r²,and change variablesy=x+sh. Tonelli applies because all terms are nonnegative. The resultingh-integral at fixeds,yis bounded byJ_r(y);integratingsgives the claimed inequality. The final lower bound follows only after inserting J_r≤C_int w². The alternative assumption J_r≤C_int w instead yields a lower bound for ∫w||∇τ||²; these are different hypotheses. If w vanishes where J_r is positive, no finite factor exists. Essential suprema avoid dependence on representatives in the interpolation parameter.',
'Takew=1andnormalize∫ρ_rdh=1.',
'ThenJ_r=1andA(r)≤4r²∫||∇τ||². A constantτhasA=0andzero gradient. The inequality goes in the useful lower-bound direction only when a positive disorderAis independently known;it cannot create a positive lower bound from the definitions alone.',
'The valid recovered chain is proved with every weight and factor visible.',
'This is a direction-field estimate,not global Navier–Stokes regularity. It supplies neither the required disorder lower bound nor control of a nonlinear production term. Its assumptions may fail at vorticity zeros or under strong intermittency.',
'Derive or falsify a uniformC_intfor the actual solution class,and state any nonvanishing or regularized direction convention before using the estimate in an enstrophy argument.',
[('Constantin and Fefferman, direction of vorticity','https://doi.org/10.1512/iumj.1993.42.42005')])
add('Misalignment is nonnegative but cannot universally control gradient energy','misalignPoly','2025-12-25','A','Fluid geometry and counterexamples','Can a two-point directional-disorder integral give an unconditional coercive bound for vorticity gradients?',
'The recovered program isolatedmisalignmentnonnegativity and left a production-versus-dissipation closure unproved. A divergence-free field with a fixed vorticity direction shows why a universal coercive lower bound cannot follow from the misalignment polynomial alone.',
['DefineM(a,b)=||a||²||b||²−(a·b)²=||a×b||²≥0.','On a2π-periodic three-torus chooseu(x,y,z)=(0,sin x,0),soω=curlu=(0,0,cos x).'],
'Exact directional-disorder counterexample','For everypairx,y,M(ω(x),ω(y))=0,but∫||∇ω||²is strictly positive. Hence no positive constantccan make a weighted two-point integral ofMonly dominatec∫||∇ω||²for all smooth divergence-free velocity fields.',
'The identity forMfollows by expanding the cross-product norm,or byCauchy–Schwarz. In the stated shear,all vorticity vectors are collinear,whether they agree,oppose,or vanish. Thus every cross product iszero and any nonnegative weighted integral ofMvanishes. However∂_xω=(0,0,−sin x),so its squared gradient integrates to(∫₀^(2π)sin²x dx)(2π)²=4π³>0. The velocity is smooth and divergence-free,so these standard kinematic assumptions do not exclude the example. This does not show a singular solution;it shows only that the proposed universal coercive inequality is false without extra hypotheses.',
'Also examine the enstrophy identity for a smooth periodicNavier–Stokes solution.',
'(1/2)d||ω||²₂/dt+ν||∇ω||²₂=∫ω·Sω,whereS=(∇u+∇u^T)/2. A bound on∫ω·Sωbyν||∇ω||²requires a separate dynamical estimate. Nonnegativity ofMdoes not supply it,and a conditional “near-field dominance” assumption must be checked rather than silently inserted.',
'The exact shear counterexample identifies the missing coercivity mechanism while preserving the valid algebraic identity.',
'The counterexample is about a proposed estimate,not a resolution of the Millennium Problem. Additional disorder,alignment or curvature hypotheses can define narrower classes,but their persistence must be proved.',
'Formulate the strongest scale-consistent conditional estimate that excludes this shear for an explicit reason,and then prove that the solution class satisfies that reason for the required time interval.',
[('Clay Mathematics Institute: Navier–Stokes','https://www.claymath.org/millennium/navier-stokes-equation/')])
add('A conditional proof chain is not a verified closure','two_point_to_gradient','2025-12-24','U','Formal logic and certification','What does a theorem proved from named regularity axioms actually establish?',
'The recoveredLeanfiles retainedaxioms and anadmitat the production-versus-dissipation step,while earlier output claimed compilation and completion. A precise logical model distinguishes a valid conditional theorem from evidence that its analytic hypotheses hold. The same distinction applies to a certifier that inserts its target matrix.',
['Suppose statementsP,Q,Rstand for disorder,intermittency and transverse regeneration,andGfor global regularity.','A theorem derivingGfrom assumptionsP,Q,Rproves(P∧Q∧R)⇒G;it does not prove the antecedent.'],
'Countermodel test for an alleged unconditional conclusion','The implication(P∧Q∧R)⇒Gcan be true even whenGis false,because the antecedent may be false. Likewise verifying eigenvalues of a hard-coded matrix certifies that matrix,not its provenance from an unavailable source operator.',
'Use a Boolean model withP=false,Q=true,R=true,G=false. The conjunction isfalse,and material implication fromfalseis true. Thus the conditional theorem can be logically valid in a model whereGfails,proving that unconditionalGdoes not follow from that implication alone. In a proof assistant,the theorem’s dependency list records the assumed constants or axioms used;compilation checks the derivation relative to them. Replacing a missing analytic estimate by an axiom moves it into the assumptions rather than solving it. For matrix certification,the same separation is algebraic:ifM₂=[[5/8,631/25000],[0,5/8]]is declared,its characteristic polynomial is(t−5/8)²and its nilpotent residual is square-zero. Those facts do not proveM₂was extracted fromCatmull–Clarkdata.',
'Apply this audit to the recoveredGC1–GC3chain and the v12 atlas certifier.',
'The output should list every unproved hypothesis and every independently supplied input. An exhaustive finite matrix test can be fully correct while the claimed source matrix remains unverified. A numerical#evalor a successful script run is also weaker than a theorem about an infinite operator.',
'The useful proof chain and finite checks can be retained with honest dependency boundaries.',
'This entry supplies a logic result and a finite matrix example,not an independentLeancompilation or a proof ofNavier–Stokesregularity. The original full files and toolchain were not recovered.',
'Produce a machine-readable axiom/dependency audit and a source-to-matrix extraction certificate,then reserve “verified” for the exact statement those artifacts establish.',
[('Lean reference manual: axioms','https://lean-lang.org/doc/reference/latest/Declarations/Axioms/')])
add('Weighted threshold rank needs a tensorial transformation law','weighted translations','2025-12-02','U','Rank and inverse problems','When does the recovered weighted-translation matrix have a basis-invariant rank,and what capacity bound follows?',
'The recoveredRGframework usedt_i=μ_i⊙ΔΦ_iandrankTas an intrinsic memory count. Ordinary rank is invariant under invertible matrix changes,but a componentwise product is coordinate-dependent unless its factors have a compatible transformation law. Sparsity identifiability requires still more information.',
['LetTbe a matrix whose columns aret_i. Rank is the dimension of their linear span.','A linear observation mapJ=BTfactors through that span and therefore hasrankJ≤rankT.'],
'Exact rank invariance and a Hadamard counterexample','rank(LTR)=rankTfor invertibleL,R. But transforming bothμandΔΦby the same invertibleLdoes not generally transformμ⊙ΔΦbyL,and can change its rank.',
'Invertible multiplication preserves the dimensions of the image and kernel,provingrankinvariance forLTR. Image(BT)⊆B(imageT)gives the rank bound. For the counterexample,take one column withμ=(1,0),ΔΦ=(0,1),so the Hadamard product iszeroandrankT=0. UseL=[[1,1],[1,−1]],which is invertible. The transformed factors are(1,1)and(1,−1),whose Hadamard product is(1,−1),so the newrankisone. Thus a claimed scheme-invariantUVcount needs a tensor or coordinate rule beyond applying the same matrix to both factors. Also rankralone does not ensure unique recovery ofr-sparse coefficients:the1×2matrix[1,1]hasrankonebut sends both distinctone-sparse vectorse₁,e₂to the same datum.',
'Compare exact rank with a numerical singular-value cutoff.',
'T=diag(1,10^(−13))has exactranktwo,but a relative threshold10^(−12)reportsone. Under a perturbation of normε,the singular values can shift by at mostε;stable numericalrankrequires an explicit gap around the threshold,not merely a chosen tolerance.',
'The valid linear factorization theorem is preserved while the coordinate and identifiability assumptions are made explicit.',
'No recoveredproof establishes the proposedSM/seesawrankorB₅capacity interpretation. A physical threshold map needs independently specified fields,weights and reparametrization rules.',
'Write the weighted map as an actual tensor contraction,then prove its covariance and analyze sparse recovery through column dependencies or spark,not rankalone.',
[('Horn and Johnson, Matrix Analysis','https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139020411')])
add('A spherical portal can cancel only specified spectral components','portal coefficients','2025-12-03','U','Harmonic analysis','What precise cancellation theorem applies to the recovered spherical-harmonic portal functional?',
'The recovered portal construction sought weights killing odd spherical modes and all degrees abovefour,then extended the idea to graphLaplacians. This is a valid projection problem once the kernel is defined. It does not require an unexplained golden-ratio determinant.',
['Use orthonormal spherical harmonicsY_l^monS²and theL²inner product.','Letcbelong to the finite-dimensional spaceV=span{Y_l^m:l=0,2,4},and defineJ(f)=⟨c,f⟩.'],
'Exact spectral cancellation and a stability bound','J annihilates every harmonic of odd degree and every degreeabovefour. For anyf∈L²,J(f)=J(P_Vf),and|J(f)−J(g)|≤||c||₂||P_V(f−g)||₂.',
'Orthogonality gives⟨Y_l^m,Y_j^n⟩=δ_ljδ_mn. Expandingcin degrees0,2,4therefore makes all excluded harmonic coefficients vanish in the pairing. Decomposef=P_Vf+(I−P_V)f;the second component is orthogonal toc,proving the identity. Cauchy–Schwarz yields the error bound. Antipodal symmetryc(−x)=c(x)alone kills odd degrees becauseY_l^m(−x)=(−1)^lY_l^m(x),but does not kill even degreesabovefour;thefinite spectral cutoff is a separate condition. The same proof works on a finite graphwith a real symmetricLaplacianand an orthonormal eigenbasis.',
'Takec=Y₀⁰+2Y₂⁰andf=3Y₀⁰+5Y₂⁰+7Y₃¹+11Y₆⁰.',
'J(f)=3+2·5=13. The odddegree-threeand evendegree-sixterms cancel for different reasons:parity and the explicit finite support. On a graph,choosingcfrom the firstthreeeigenvectors similarly annihilates all other eigenspaces;the numerical ordering must account for repeated eigenvalues.',
'The portal becomes a reproducible linear functional with exact cancellation and a sharp perturbation estimate.',
'The full historical4×4matrix field and annulus integral were not recovered,so no claimedφcancellation or numerical portal table is inferred. A changing graphrequires tracking its eigenspaces and spectral gaps.',
'Provide the actual matrix-valuedfield,define its scalar observable independently,and compute its harmonic coefficients before designing the projection kernel.',
[('NIST DLMF spherical harmonics','https://dlmf.nist.gov/14.30')])
add('Greedy spectral deflation converges to zero in trace norm','Original question: conditions','2025-12-03','U','Compact operators','Which clearly specified deflation process has a complete finite-rank convergence theorem?',
'The recovered iteration chose a top eigenspace of an accumulated covariance,which is different from simply removing the current largest eigenvalues. A precise current-covariance model has an exact theorem and clarifies why a nonzero residual or a fixed limiting subspace cannot be assumed.',
['LetΣ₀≥0be trace class with orthonormal eigenvectorse_jand decreasing eigenvaluesλ_j≥0.','At each step letP_nproject onto the nextpuncut eigenvectors and defineΣ_(n+1)=(I−P_n)Σ_n(I−P_n).'],
'Exact trace-norm tail formula','After nsteps,Σ_n=Σ_(j>np)λ_je_j⊗e_jand||Σ_n||₁=Σ_(j>np)λ_j→0. In finite dimension the process terminates after at mostceiling(d/p)steps.',
'The projection is diagonal in the same eigenbasis asΣ_nand removes exactly the selectedpterms. Induction gives the displayed expansion. For a positive trace-classoperator,the trace norm equals the sum of its nonnegative eigenvalues,so thetailformula follows. Summability ofΣλ_jmakes thattailtend tozero. This proves a stronger convergence than strong-operator convergence. If the operator is merely compact,the largest remaining eigenvalue tends tozeroand operator-norm convergence still follows,but trace-norm statements need not make sense. Selecting the top eigenspace of an accumulatedsumcan repeatedly select already removed modes or requiretie rules;the samebatch formula cannot be copied to that different algorithm.',
'TakeΣ₀=diag(1,1/2,1/4,1/8,…),p=1.',
'After nsteps,the trace norm isΣ_(j>n)2^(1−j)=2^(1−n). Every residual direction is eventually removed,and the limit iszero. The selectedrank-oneprojectorsmove through the basis rather than converging in operator normto a fixedrank-oneprojector;their pairwise norm distance isone.',
'The revised model has exact convergence and shows which extra claims about a limiting subspace need separate proofs.',
'This is explicitly a newly specifiedcurrent-spectrumdeflation model,not a proof that the recovered cumulative-history iteration obeys it. The latter needs its full discrete/continuous history convention and tie-breaking rule.',
'For the actual history-based iteration,derive scalar score dynamics under simultaneous diagonalizability and prove eventual removal of every positive mode before claiming an operator orGrassmannianlimit.',
[('Simon, Trace Ideals','https://bookstore.ams.org/surv-120')])
add('Cumulant evolution is triangular for an actual OU process','cumulant propagation','2025-12-10','U','Probability and differential equations','What exact cumulant theorem can replace the proposed unproved first-cumulant/eigenvalue controller?',
'The recovered engine used formalStirling–Bernoullimaps as if they automatically described stochastic cumulants. For a specifiedlinear diffusion,the cumulants do obey an exact triangular system,but changing its mean does not alter its relaxation eigenvalue. This provides a clear positive model and a sharp limit.',
['LetdX=−λXdt+bdt+√εσdWwithλ>0and an initial moment-generating function nearzero.','DefineK(s,t)=logE[e^(sX_t)]=Σ_(n≥1)κ_n(t)s^n/n!nearzero.'],
'Exact OU cumulant equations','κ₁′=−λκ₁+b,κ₂′=−2λκ₂+εσ²,andκ_n′=−nλκ_nforn≥3. In particular changingbonly shifts the mean and leavesλand the variance-relaxation rate2λunchanged.',
'The generator applied toe^(sx)is(−λsx+bs+(εσ²/2)s²)e^(sx). Under the stated local exponential integrability,differentiating its expectation gives∂_tM=−λs∂_sM+bsM+(εσ²/2)s²M. Divide byMto obtain∂_tK=−λs∂_sK+bs+(εσ²/2)s². Compare powers ofsusing the exponential-generating normalization:the linear term givesκ₁′,the quadratic term givesκ₂′,and no newhighercumulantsare forced. Equivalently the explicitOUsolutionis an affine image ofX₀plus an independentGaussian;the same equations follow from cumulant additivity and scaling.',
'Takeλ=σ=1andb=3.',
'The stationary mean isthreeand varianceε/2;all stationaryhighercumulantsvanish. Replacingbbyfourchanges only the mean. It cannot move the drift Jacobian from−1to another eigenvalue. Any claimed first-cumulantcontrollerof a spectral escape rate therefore needs a different,explicit coupling mechanism.',
'The stochastic cumulantpropagationis proved for a genuine process,and the missing control assumption is isolated.',
'This does not identify the singularStirling–Bernoullimatrixwith theOUgeneratororFeigenbaumrenormalization. For nonlinear drifts,highermomentsgenerally couple upward and finite closure is an approximation unless proved.',
'For a nonlinear model,derive its exact generator moment hierarchy,then quantify a truncation error before using a finite cumulant map for rate control.',
[('Øksendal, Stochastic Differential Equations','https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-14394-6')])
